  title: Hyderabad under the Nizams
  text: Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah founded the state of Hyderabad in 1724 as Mughal governor of the Deccan. The Nizams became allies of the British and ruled until 1948, when Hyderabad joined India.
